\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 1. Mandatory Project Inspection\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Before implementation, thoroughly inspect the entire existing VHSart project.\
Identify and document:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Existing horizontal tracking and tear engines.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal line and segment noise generators.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Green/chroma noise capabilities.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Static and signal noise engines.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Frame displacement, wrapping, and sampling utilities.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Base image processing, softness, grain, and compositing systems.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Existing temporal animation and deterministic seed infrastructure.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Preset registration and parameter UI architecture.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Reuse existing functionality wherever appropriate. Extend existing engines instead of duplicating them.\
However, do not force unrelated effects into one generic engine. This preset needs its own temporal orchestration and dedicated combination logic.\
Do not break, replace, or alter unrelated presets.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 2. Core Visual Identity\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Reconstruct the reference as a multi-stage analog signal failure sequence.\
The effect must transition through several visually distinct states:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Phase 1 \'97 Initial Horizontal Tracking Damage
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 Approximate reference interval: 00:00.000\'9600:00.500.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Medium-gray background.\
{\listtext	\'95	}A localized horizontal interference/tear band near the middle.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Fragmented horizontal dark lines.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Occasional short white and gray interruptions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Moderate signal instability.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Phase 2 \'97 Green-Dominant Horizontal Static
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 Approximate reference interval: 00:01.000\'9600:02.500.\
This is the dominant visual phase.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Dense horizontal segmented noise across the frame.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Strong green color dominance.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Mixtures of green, dark, white, gray, and occasional muted purple/blue.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Short and medium horizontal segments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Per-frame flickering and changing segment positions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Localized RGB/chroma displacement.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Limited horizontal chroma bleeding associated with the streaks.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregular luminance flashes and dropouts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Avoid turning this into generic green film grain or a uniform green tint.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Phase 3 \'97 Temporary Signal Stabilization
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 Approximate reference time: 00:03.000.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Return to a relatively uniform medium-gray base.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Reduce the dense green static substantially.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Retain subtle neutral signal noise.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Introduce fragmented horizontal interference concentrated near the lower edge.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Allow a small, occasional green artifact near the upper region.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Phase 4 \'97 Upper Tracking Tear & Frame Shift
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 Approximate reference time: 00:03.500.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}A dark and light fragmented horizontal interference band near the upper region.\
{\listtext	\'95	}A brighter gray field below it.\
{\listtext	\'95	}A narrow displaced or cut-looking boundary near the left side.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Optional horizontal/vertical frame displacement or wrapping.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregular line interruptions and tracking instability.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 These phases must preserve their distinct visual identities.\
The approximate timestamps describe the supplied reference, not hardcoded animation triggers.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 3. Dedicated Multi-Phase Architecture\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement a dedicated:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Multi-Phase Tracking & Green Static Engine
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
It must coordinate three independently controllable subsystems.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 A. Green-Dominant Horizontal Static System\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Responsible for the main dense green noise phase.\
Requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Procedural horizontal segmented noise.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Variable segment lengths and thicknesses.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Green-dominant chromatic distribution.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Secondary white, black, gray, and muted purple/blue components.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Independent luminance and chroma variation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Per-frame flickering.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Configurable horizontal density and segment distribution.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Subtle horizontal chroma displacement.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Limited streak-associated chroma bleeding.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Generate the pattern mathematically. Do not use image overlays or pre-rendered noise.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 B. Horizontal Tear & Tracking Band System\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Responsible for the initial middle tear, dark horizontal lines, lower-edge dropouts, and final upper tear.\
Requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Configurable band position and height.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal row displacement.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Fragmented dark and bright horizontal lines.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Variable line lengths and thicknesses.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregular band boundaries.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Independent luminance disruption.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Multiple independently positioned bands where supported.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal changes in position, intensity, and segmentation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The system must support upper, middle, and lower placement without forcing all bands to appear simultaneously.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 C. Frame Shift & Boundary Displacement System\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Responsible for the final phase\'92s visible left-side boundary and frame displacement.\
Requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal frame shift.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Vertical frame shift.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Optional wrapping.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Configurable edge behavior.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Cropping and displaced-boundary artifacts.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Optional activation during selected temporal phases.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not apply continuous full-frame displacement when the reference only shows localized or phase-specific movement.\
Handle RGB and alpha sampling consistently.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 4. Temporal Phase Orchestration\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement a dedicated temporal phase controller.\
The controller must calculate phase weights and coordinate the subsystems.\
Conceptually:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}trackingBandWeight(t)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\ls10\ilvl0
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}greenStaticWeight(t)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\ls10\ilvl0
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}stabilizationWeight(t)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\ls10\ilvl0
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}upperTearWeight(t)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\ls10\ilvl0
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}frameShiftWeight(t)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Use smooth or deliberately abrupt transitions according to the visual behavior of each phase.\
The reference contains noticeable changes between signal states. Do not reduce the entire clip to one continuously active noise layer.\
Provide three temporal operating modes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Automatic Phase Evolution
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 procedural evolution of the different signal damage states.\
\ls11\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	2.	}Manual Phase Control
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 user-controlled phase selection and timing.\
\ls11\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	3.	}Frozen State
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 freezes the generated pattern and phase state for a stable frame.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Support adjustable phase timing and transition duration.\
Use the supplied reference timestamps as initial calibration guidance only. Do not hardcode the effect to a fixed 4.163-second duration or assume that every composition has the same frame rate.\
The effect must work correctly when the user changes composition duration, frame rate, and render position.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 5. Procedural Noise and Deterministic Randomness\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Use deterministic hash-based procedural generation.\
The effective random state must depend on:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}User Seed.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Composition time or frame identity.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Selected temporal mode.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Relevant subsystem identity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Repeatable rendering of the same frame.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Stable results independent of render-call order.\
{\listtext	\'95	}No global mutable random generator.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Thread-safe operation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}MFR compatibility.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Independent random distributions for different subsystems.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Changing the seed should create a different variation while preserving the overall visual identity and phase behavior.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 6. Base Signal and Image Quality\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Reuse VHSart\'92s existing base-processing engines wherever appropriate.\
The reference includes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls14\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Medium-gray and light-gray base states.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Low-resolution analog softness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Subtle neutral grain.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Reduced high-frequency detail.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Darker signal regions during intense interference.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Keep the base signal independently controllable from the green static and tracking systems.\
Do not add unnecessary paper textures, artificial film scratches, or unrelated VHS artifacts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

